# Installed scanner and explicit local rules only. One whole-repository job.
name: Standalone Semgrep keeps partial coverage through selection and restart
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN SEMGREP_AGENT_TOKEN
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/standalone_partial.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/alpha-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 RESULT READY | imported-map
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Scan | accepted-map
keys: Escape
paste-file: @ART/standalone-scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/standalone_partial.py @TMP_TARGET @ART unselected
submit: workbench
nav-mode:
require-live-snap: 30 RESULT partial | partial-120x36
expect: Incomplete coverage
expect: incompatible-fixture-rule
ask: Does standalone Scan disclose its partial outcome, actual omitted rule and retained finding before explicit acknowledgement?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 15 Incomplete coverage | partial-160x48
ask: At 160x48, does standalone partial coverage remain distinct from a complete discovery result?
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 15 Incomplete coverage | partial-96x89
ask: At 96x89, is the recorded standalone result readable without accepting or starting work?
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 15 u Accept partial | partial-80x24
ask: At 80x24, are partial coverage and the explicit acceptance control understandable?
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 15 u Accept partial | partial-60x20
ask: At 60x20, can the operator read the retained result and control its acceptance?
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 u Accept | partial-40x12
ask: At 40x12, do partial status, reading controls and explicit acceptance remain reachable?
keys: NPage NPage NPage
require-live-snap: 15 10-13/13 | partial-40x12-paged
ask: Do the displayed paging controls actually move the standalone evidence without accepting it?
resize: 120x36
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Review | acknowledged-standalone
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/standalone_partial.py @TMP_TARGET @ART selected
expect: 1 remaining
keys: Escape
paste-file: @ART/open-finding.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 needs_review | retained-observation
submit: dismiss false_positive Labeled local rule fixture
require-live-snap: 25 rejected_false_positive | reviewed-observation
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 1 findings · 1 reviewed | standalone-report
ask: Can the retained observation reach Report after a human decision while review completeness stays separate from coverage?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scan
nav-mode:
require-live-snap: 25 Incomplete coverage | restarted-scan
expect: partial acknowledged
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/standalone_partial.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: After restart without color, are standalone partial coverage, explicit acknowledgement and retained evidence readable without another scan?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
